# Devices

::summary
The Devices hub destination in the shell wrapper: F-12 groups (This Workspace / Model Servers (Advanced) / Deploy lanes) with status-pill rows and Add Device enrollment. Device rows link the per-device PAGE at `/devices/{id}` (08-24 device-pages round, items 4 + 12 — a real route, not a sheet): live status, the details the store already holds (name, platform, presence, capabilities, last seen), and — gated on the advertised `fs` capability AND the device being online — a read-only file browser driven by the server relay (`{capability fs, method list_dir|read}`), navigated with `?path=` / `?file=` query hrefs exactly like the app-detail code tree. Offline, no-`fs`, an unrecognised agent answer and a too-large or non-text file each render their OWN honest state — never a fake affordance. The page rides this wrapper (`tab=main`); `modals/device-detail.surf` stays the small-width capability sheet. Lane rows open the deploy-lane detail surface. The enroll-device and add-model-server sheets live in `modals/` — no inline copies.
::

